  "description": "The general election for Illinois's 6th Congressional District pits incumbent Democrat Sean Casten against Republican nominee Niki Conforti in a rematch of their 2024 contest. The district encompasses Chicago's southwestern suburbs including Downers Grove, Wheaton, Lisle, Orland Park, and parts of Chicago proper, with a Cook Partisan Voting Index of D+3. The March 17, 2026 primaries are complete, with Casten defeating Joseph Ruzevich and Conforti defeating Skylar Duensing. Nonpartisan forecasters (Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, Sabato's Crystal Ball) all rate this seat as Solid/Safe Democratic heading into the general election.",
